# Every text file in this repo is stored with LF and checked out with LF on every computer, whatever
# core.autocrlf says (Git for Windows ships core.autocrlf=true). Added with no churn: renormalizing the
# repo under this line changed no file (2026-11-14). Binary files are detected and left alone.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The time tracker build mm-hooks carries is checked byte for byte against the sha256 values in
# plugins/mm-hooks/extension.json, by plugins/mm-hooks/scripts/sync-extension.js on every teammate's
# computer and by scripts/carry-extension.mjs in a release. Git for Windows ships core.autocrlf=true,
# which would rewrite every text file here to CRLF on checkout (the marketplace clone Claude Code makes
# and every plugin cache copy taken from it) and fail that check, so the tracker never updated on
# Windows. -text: git never converts line endings in these files, on checkout or on commit, so the
# working tree holds exactly the published bytes (fonts/OFL.txt is published with mixed line endings).
# These lines come after the * line on purpose: the later line wins.
plugins/mm-hooks/extension/** -text
plugins/mm-hooks/extension.json -text
